WEBVTT

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:01.620
Click Manager Dashboard

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:02.640
in the left sidebar.

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:04.740
Start with the reporting period.

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:06.110
Choose Today,

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:08.000
This Week or This Month.

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:09.670
Use the same period

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:10.850
when comparing activity.

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:12.690
Read the label

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:13.710
on each number.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.620
Posting activity, active

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:17.280
listings and sold reporting

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:18.660
tell you different things.

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:20.380
A reported sale

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:21.600
is useful context,

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:23.460
but that number alone doesn't

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:24.860
explain what led to it.

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:26.210
If a teammate's

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:27.390
activity looks low,

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:29.050
start with a simple question.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:30.460
What happened

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:31.480
with your last post?

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:32.850
Ask them

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:34.190
to open Post to Market

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:35.490
and show you the Queue.

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:37.380
If the task stopped,

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:38.700
check the connection

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.080
and inventory together.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.000
Can't find the page?

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:44.790
Go to Configuration, then Team,

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:46.030
and check their access.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:48.280
If the setup is ready

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:49.600
but a step is unclear,

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:51.200
replay that lesson.

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:52.890
Let the teammate show

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:54.000
you the step afterwards.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:56.240
Agree on one useful

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:58.280
next action, such as checking

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:00.060
a failed row or confirming

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.080
the correct inventory.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:03.060
Follow up on that

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:04.420
action during the next shift.

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:06.620
In your workbook,

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:07.640
choose a reporting

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:09.260
period and one metric.

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:10.900
Write the question you

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:12.030
would ask, and the next

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:13.410
task you would check together.
